# FIRE repo map

FIRE ENGINE (Failure Investigation & Root Explanation) diagnoses incidents in watched systems
from payload shapes and process paths, never raw values. Hexagonal; the package is `fire/`.
Rules naming a `panoptes/` package or `config/panoptes.yml` describe Panoptes, another repo,
and do not apply here.

| Path | What lives there |
|---|---|
| `fire/core/domain/` | Pydantic models, and the `Baseline`, `Path`, and `CompleteFlow` dataclasses: `dossier` (`Shape`, `ShapeField`, `ValueType`, `ShapeFingerprint`, `ProcessHop`, `HopVia`, `ProcessPath`, `EvidenceFragment`, `Dossier`), `decision` (`Possibility`, `Decision`), `incident` (`Incident`, `Trigger`), `narration`, `origin`, `inventory` (`SystemInventory`, `CoverageReport`), `observation` (`Channel`, `ShapeObservation`, `SpanObservation`, `SpanLink`, `StreamSummary`, `FingerprintSummary`), `ingest` (`IngestReport`, `IngestCounts`, `Rejection`, `RejectionReason`), `envelope` (`Envelope`, `ValuePath`, `TimestampPath`, `PayloadPath`), `baseline` (`DriftPolicy`, `BaselineStatus`, `Baseline`), `drift` (`FieldRef`, `TypeChange`, `ShapeDiff`, `DriftSignal`, `Admission`, `ShapeAdmission`), `flow` (`PathPolicy`, the system YAML's `paths`; `Node`, `FlowCounters`, `ShapeRef`, `FlowAssembler`: spans and shapes into open flows; `CompleteFlow`: entry, local roots, reach, shape attachment, `process_path`), `path` (`Path`, `settle`: a complete flow's outcome and path drift; `PathDriftRule`, `PathDriftSignal`, `PathDriftFiring`, `PathDrift`, `FlowOutcome`, and the `/paths` models `PathsReport`, `PathSummary`, `NodeSummary`, `EdgeSummary`), `route_template` (`RouteTemplate`, `Route`, `RouteTable`, `best_template`: a request path to its route template), `operation` (`OperationNamer`, `OperationInputs`, `OperationName`, the id rules, and `OperationRules` and `HostRule`, the system YAML's `operations`), `capture` (`CaptureRule`, `CaptureLayout`, `CaptureEvent`: the system YAML's capture rules and `capture_event`; `read_capture_key`, `checked_action`, `object_key`, and `CaptureIndex` with `SpanRef`: capture keys to the span that named them) |
| `fire/core/ports/` | Protocols: `Reasoner`, `Narrator`, `Notifier`, `ObservationCatalog`, `ShapeGeneralizer`, `ShapeFingerprinter`, `ManifestParser`, `RecordSource` (with `RawRecord`, `StartPosition`), `ExchangeSource` (with `ExchangeSink`, `HttpExchange`, `HttpMessage`, and its skip and note reasons), `SpanSource` (with `SpanSink`, `RawSpan`, `RawLink`, `SpanBatchResult`, `SpanRequestNote`), `CaptureSource` (with `RawCapture`, `ObjectState`) |
| `fire/core/services/` | `DiagnosisService` (reasoner, then narrator, then notifier), `IngestService` (checks and stores observations; `ingest` takes an `on_drift` hook per call and calls it once per new drift signal), `DriftIncidentService` (one incident and dossier per new shape drift signal, and per flow that fires a new path drift signal), `RecordPipeline` (raw record to `ShapeObservation` or a reason code), `ExchangePipeline` (HTTP exchange to request and response `ShapeObservation`s or reason codes), `SpanPipeline` (received span to `SpanObservation` and its client bodies to outbound `ShapeObservation`s, or reason codes), `CapturePipeline` (capture pair to outbound request and response `ShapeObservation`s joined through the capture index, or reason codes), and `coverage` (`audit_coverage`, `CoverageScope`) |
| `fire/adapters/shapes/` | `FlatStarShapeGeneralizer` (JSON to `Shape`), `Sha256ShapeFingerprinter` |
| `fire/adapters/manifests/` | `EventChainsGraphParser` (`event_chains_graph` document to `SystemInventory`), `openapi_routes` (OpenAPI 3 document to `Route`s) |
| `fire/adapters/sources/` | `RecordSource` adapters: `ReplayRecordSource` (`.json`, `.jsonl`, or a directory). `ExchangeSource` adapters: `HttpProxy` (inbound reverse proxy: uvicorn in front, `httpcore` to the upstream). `SpanSource` adapters: `OtlpReceiver` (OTLP/HTTP JSON, `POST /v1/traces`) and `parse_traces` with the attribute allowlist and capture events. `CaptureSource` adapters: `S3CaptureSource` (lists each prefix's `responses/` and reads pairs once settled; boto3 through threads) and `make_s3_client`. `listener.py`: `listen` and the quiet uvicorn server both listeners use |
| `fire/adapters/memory/` | `MemoryObservationCatalog`: observations, baselines, open flows, and paths per system, on an injectable clock; in-process, lost on restart |
| `fire/adapters/{reasoners,narrators,notifiers}/` | Stubs: `EchoReasoner`, `TemplateNarrator`, `ConsoleNotifier` |
| `fire/apps/config.py` | YAML to Pydantic: `FireConfig` (`config/fire.yml`, with `TentacleConfig`), `SystemConfig` (`config/systems/*.yml`, with one source model per `kind`) |
| `fire/apps/discovery.py` | `discover`: per system, an inventory from its manifest or a `missing_reason` |
| `fire/apps/env.py` | `load_fire_env`: loads `.env`; process env wins |
| `fire/apps/incident_engine/` | The body. `app.py` (FastAPI: `GET /health`, `POST /v0/diagnose`, `POST /v0/observations`, which opens shape drift incidents, `GET /v0/systems/{system}/streams`, `GET /v0/systems/{system}/paths`; a loop in the lifespan completes settled flows every second and opens path drift incidents), `wiring.py` (`build_container`, with an optional clock; `log_drift`, `log_path_drift`), `__main__.py` |
| `fire/apps/tentacle/` | `python -m fire.apps.tentacle --system <system>`: `runner.py` (startup checks, run loop, exit codes), `sender.py` (batches of shapes and spans, retries), `counters.py`, `sources.py` (`READERS` by kind, `open_http_proxy`, `open_otlp_receiver`, `open_s3_capture`). One `CaptureIndex` per run, filled by receivers and read by capture sources |
| `config/fire.yml` | Global: API token env var, reasoner, narrator, notifier, tier budgets, tentacle sending |
| `config/systems/` | One YAML per watched system; `_template.yml` is skipped. `omg.yml` is OMG, the first |
| `dev/omg/` | OMG's local stack with FIRE attached (L2): `README.md` (commands), `compose.fire.yml` and `otel-collector-config.yml` (one more collector exporter, to the tentacle), `record_otlp.py` (records the collector's exports, scrubbed, as L1 fixtures), `record_captures.py` (records transmission captures from LocalStack's bucket, scrubbed, as L1 fixtures) |
| `tests/unit/` | Flat `test_<topic>.py` files |
| `tests/integration/` | API and tentacle tests; the body through `TestClient` or `httpx.ASGITransport`, with config written to `tmp_path` |
| `tests/conftest.py` | The `canary` and `quiet_httpx` fixtures; skips `omg_local` tests unless `OMG_REPO` is set |
| `tests/canary.py` | Canary harness: `Canary` plants unique values and finds leaks; `WIRE_FORMS` per source kind |
| `tests/otlp_json.py` | Builders of OTLP JSON trace requests, as a collector's `otlphttp` exporter writes them |
| `tests/spans.py` | Builders of `SpanObservation`s and order flows for flow and path tests, and `Clock`, the body's clock moved by hand |
| `tests/fixtures/omg/` | L1 fixtures: `test_payloads/` is copied unchanged from OMG's synthetic test data; `api_requests/` holds request bodies with placeholder values that keep each value type (an `omg_local` test checks the shape matches OMG's); `openapi/` holds the `paths` and operation ids of the `/openapi.json` of OMG's API and validation engine (an `omg_local` test checks them against the live documents); `otlp/` holds two recordings of what OMG's collector exported for a place order, scrubbed by `dev/omg/record_otlp.py`; `captures/` holds transmission capture pairs per client label, `helios/` recorded by `dev/omg/record_captures.py` and `oracle-om/` and `insurance/` derived from OMG's client models |

